clueweb09-en0002-67-12406.150 gsmd fails to recognize network registration atcmd.c:210:ml_parse() buf=`+CREG: 2'(8) Sun Aug 26 14:21:42 2007 <1> atcmd.c:278:ml_parse() extd reply `+CREG: 2' to cmd `+COPS=0', must be unsolicited After that, +COPS=0 is endlessly sent, and gsmd eventually declares the modem dead. GTA01Bv4, P0 developer version. Anyone know what's going on here? Why isn't the +CREG being matched as a response to the +COPS ? -- Rod > Sun Aug 26 14:21:17 2007 <6> log.c:106:gsmdlog_init() logfile successfully opened > Sun Aug 26 14:21:17 2007 <1> machine.c:131:gsmd_machine_plugin_init() detected 'GTA01' hardware > Sun Aug 26 14:21:17 2007 <1> machine.c:72:gsmd_machine_plugin_load() loading machine plugin "generic" > Sun Aug 26 14:21:17 2007 <1> vendor.c:75:gsmd_vendor_plugin_load()
